<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PathAssistant xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        The DIRECT, UNLISTED disposition path, for the Off_Market record type.
        Seven steps: Disposition Readiness, NDA, Disposition Offer, LOI, PSA, Closing,
        Completed. No broker is engaged, so there is no BOV Outreach, no Active Listing and
        no Call for Offers - those three are restricted out of the Off_Market value set.

        Completed is copied BYTE-IDENTICAL - fieldNames AND info text - from the
        now-deactivated Disposition_Path. Closing was too until 2026-08-09, when the code
        review's C1 finding added a third sentence to it (fieldNames unchanged, the original
        two sentences unchanged): complete the wire verification BEFORE submitting the Closing
        approval. That ordering is not a preference - Closing_Approval sets recordEditability
        AdminOnly, so while it is pending the Disposition is locked and
        Wire_Verification_Rollup cannot write the flag (it now fails soft rather than rolling
        the Wire save back). The IDENTICAL sentence is on Disposition_Path_On_Market's Closing
        step - these two must stay in step with each other.

        Disposition Readiness is the ONE deliberate exception to that carry-over, corrected on
        request 2026-08-09. The original text ended "before advancing to BOV Outreach", which
        is on-market wording: BOV Outreach does not exist on this path at all, which goes
        Readiness -> NDA. The trailing clause now names NDA. Its fieldNames (Property_Asset__c)
        and the rest of the sentence are unchanged, and the On_Market copy of this step still
        carries the original wording, which is correct there.

        🔴 THE "NOT CORRECTED, DELIBERATELY" NOTE THAT STOOD HERE IS RETRACTED - 2026-08-10,
        BY D27.1 / D28-Q2. It is quoted rather than deleted because this file's copy was one of
        three that told the next reader to leave a known-wrong clock alone, and three copies of
        that instruction are what made this a review blocker rather than a one-line fix:

            RETRACTED: "NOT corrected, deliberately: the Active Listing step text on the
            On_Market path ("6-week marketing clock ... Week 4 YELLOW ... Week 6 Hard Stop") is
            under an OPEN user question about a 2-month vs 6-week clock. That step does not
            exist on this path, but do not "fix" it on the other one either."

        (Those milestone names survive above ONLY as a verbatim quotation of retracted text.)

        WHAT ANSWERED IT: D27.1 - THE DOCUMENT WON. The marketing period is 60 days with a
        30-day traction checkpoint, and traction is logged offers and NOTHING else (D28-Q1).
        The Active Listing text on Disposition_Path_On_Market and on the deactivated
        Disposition_Path was rewritten to that model in this change, and the bands both now
        name are DispositionTractionService's.

        NOTHING IN THIS FILE CHANGED BUT THIS COMMENT, for the reason the retracted note gave
        and the opening paragraph still gives: Active Listing is restricted out of the
        Off_Market value set, so this path has no Active Listing step to correct. The paragraph
        is kept only so a reader of this file is not left holding the retracted instruction.

        NDA, Disposition Offer, LOI and PSA are new, text-only steps: none has a
        Disposition__c field to surface. Nothing about NDA__c itself changes in this tranche -
        no new values, no rename, no Party_Role__c.

        Step ORDER in this file is the design's path order for readability. Runtime display
        order comes from the Disposition_Stage__c picklist value order (sorted=false).
    -->
    <active>true</active>
    <entityName>Disposition__c</entityName>
    <fieldName>Disposition_Stage__c</fieldName>
    <masterLabel>Disposition Path Off Market</masterLabel>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Property_Asset__c</fieldNames>
        <info>Confirm the asset metrics and Argus signal support the sell decision before advancing to NDA.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Disposition Readiness</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>Send an NDA to each interested party. Create one NDA record per party using the NDA lookup to this Disposition. The expanded NDA model - the Declined state, the Pending to Not Sent rename, party roles, counter-signature and the all-signed gate - arrives in a later change; until then track each NDA Status by hand.</info>
        <picklistValueName>NDA</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>Offers are captured on Disposition Offer records against this Disposition. Log the buyer name, offer amount, financing type, due-diligence and closing periods, then work the counter fields until an offer is accepted.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Disposition Offer</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>LOI is a phase of this disposition, not a separate record - the disposition-side LOI record arrives in a later change. Until then the negotiation stays on the Disposition Offer record: drive it through Offer Status and the DPEG Counter Price, DPEG Counter Date, Buyer Counter Price and Final Agreed Price fields.</info>
        <picklistValueName>LOI</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>PSA is a phase of this disposition, not a separate record - the disposition-side contract has no record yet and arrives in a later change. PSA Executed on this Disposition is the only marker; tick it on the Closing step once the purchase and sale agreement is signed.</info>
        <picklistValueName>PSA</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>PSA_Executed__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Title_Company__c</fieldNames>
        <info>PSA Executed = TRUE spawns closing tasks. Wire fraud prevention gate (6 fields) must be complete before wiring. Complete the wire verification BEFORE submitting the Closing approval - the approval locks this Disposition, so a Wire saved while it is pending will not update the Wire Verification Completed flag until the approval resolves.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Closing</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Closing_Date__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Net_Sale_Proceeds__c</fieldNames>
        <info>Deal closed. Confirm the closing date, net sale proceeds, and that the closing statement is on file.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Completed</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <recordTypeName>Off_Market</recordTypeName>
</PathAssistant>
